# NOTE: git does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line. A line like
#   .env    # my token
# is read as a pattern containing spaces and a '#', and matches nothing. Keep
# every comment on its own line. (This bit us once, caught by bin/_publishcheck.sh.)

# --- secrets and personal data: never commit ---------------------------------
# HF_TOKEN, optionally ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
.env
# your device names and your label — ship config.example.yaml instead
config.yaml
# your product, customer and colleague names — ship glossary.example.md instead
glossary.md
glossary-candidates.md
# yayın taramasında aranan kuruma özel adların listesi — bu da gizli
.publishcheck-patterns
*.local.yaml

# --- local-only working notes (customer/personal detail) ----------------------
# the public, sanitised version of these is ENGINEERING-NOTES.md
CLAUDE.md
TEST-OKUMA-METNI.md

# --- runtime state ------------------------------------------------------------
.state.json
.autostart-enabled
.autostart-snooze
.autostart-cooldown
.limit-next
.menubar.lock
progress.json
timeline.json
mic.parts.json

# --- recordings and outputs ---------------------------------------------------
# Meetings live in paths.meetings_dir (~/Meetings by default), outside the repo.
# These patterns are a safety net in case anyone points it at the project folder.
*.wav
*.ffmpeg.log
guard.log
process.log
stop.log
*-transcript.md
*-transcript.json
*-transcript.raw.md
*-corrections.md
*-action-items.md
*.superseded.md

# --- python / macOS -----------------------------------------------------------
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.update-check.json
